    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-bcd6503daa24] states the subject (the new `frontend.max-metadata-cache-freshness` config key), the change (added) and its purpose: it sets a time window in which recent metadata results are not cached, so stale results are not returned. Nothing is said to break if the operator does nothing. The same release section shows that caching of /series and /labels results is itself new in 3.0.0 [ev-af3b569bbd49]. So the new option only tunes a metadata cache that is also new, and the open applicability aspect can be written as opt-in: no existing behaviour is exposed. The default value is not given, which is why confidence is low.",
